==================================================
14. CHOOSING THE RIGHT CHART
==================================================

Line Plot
→ Best for trends and changes over time.

Bar Chart
→ Best for comparing categories.

Histogram
→ Best for frequency distributions.

Scatter Plot
→ Best for relationships between two variables.

Pie Chart
→ Best for showing parts of a whole.

Box Plot
→ Best for distribution, spread and outliers.

Area Chart
→ Best for showing trends with filled regions.

Heatmap
→ Best for showing values through color intensity.

Subplots
→ Best for displaying multiple charts together.


==================================================
15. KEY TAKEAWAYS
==================================================

- Matplotlib is widely used for Python data visualization.
- Different charts are suitable for different types of data.
- Labels and titles make graphs easier to understand.
- Customization improves chart readability.
- Scatter plots help study relationships.
- Histograms show data distribution.
- Box plots can reveal outliers.
- Heatmaps represent values using color intensity.
- Subplots allow multiple visualizations in one figure.
- Seaborn can be used with Matplotlib for advanced visualizations.